            <div xml:id="d38">

                <pb facs="0124" n="38" sameAs="frus:frus1927v01/pg38"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15 a 1/216: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Houghton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-05-06T13:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 6, 1927—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 6—8:56 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>105. Your 93, May 5, noon. Chamberlain assures me that British delegation at the
                    forthcoming Three-Power Conference will include fully empowered Dominion
                    representatives.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Houghton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
